> I made the tests changig the values in the sound/pci/hda/patch_nvhdmi.c f=
ile
> manually.
> To summarize the results i have perfect sound up to 192khz/32bits(S32_LE
> format). But only one configuration at a time.
> =

> How can we set multiple formats here, or let the system pass all formats =
to
> the av receiver ?
> =

> Here are the detailed results i tested.
> =

> In the source code
> =A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 .rates =3D SNDRV_PCM_RATE_A
> =A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 .maxbps =3D B,
> =A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 .formats =3D SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_SC_LE,

Change like

	.rates =3D SNDRV_PCM_RATE_A | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_B | ...,
	.maxbps =3D 24,
	.formats =3D SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_A | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_B | ...,

> 1. A=3D192000, B=3D24, C=3D16,=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 perfect sound, with speaker=
-test -Dhdmi -c6
> -r192000 -FS16_LE, no other setting working
> 2. A=3D 192000, B=3D24, C=3D32,=A0=A0=A0=A0 perfect sound, with speaker-t=
est -Dhdmi -c6
> -r192000 -FS32_LE, no other setting working
> 3. A=3D 96000, B=3D24, C=3D32,=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 perfect sound, with spea=
ker-test -Dhdmi -c6=A0
> -r96000 -FS32_LE, no other setting working
> 4. A=3D192000, B=3D24, C=3D24,=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 strange high pitched sound =
from all speakers,
> with speaker-test -Dhdmi -c6 -r192000 -FS24_LE, no other settings working
> 5. A=3D=A0 96000, B=3D24, C=3D24,=A0=A0=A0=A0=A0 strange high pitched sou=
nd from all speakers,
> with speaker-test -Dhdmi -c6 -r96000 -FS24_LE, no other settings working

S24_LE is no format for HD-audio.  It's 24bit packed in lower 3 bytes
of 4 byte frame.  For 24bit format, use S32_LE.


